---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Join from "~app/join";

const title = "Join Shoal — Set up your station";
const description =
  "Use Shoal's staged Join journey to set up your station and Review Policy.";
const joinServiceUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SHOAL_JOIN_SERVICE_URL
  ?? (import.meta.env.DEV ? "http://127.0.0.1:8787" : "");
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="wrap guide-page join-page">
    <header class="join-intro">
      <p class="section-kicker">BECOME A REVIEWER</p>
      <h1>Join Shoal</h1>
      <p>
        Shoal is a public review network where repository owners request
        evaluation from independent Reviewers, and passing reviews can make
        real GitHub Stars explainable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your station. Your Review Policy. Directly fork the Shoal station template to
        join.
      </p>
      <p class="join-reassurance">
        Public browsing · Optional GitHub authorization · Your standard
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="reviewer-lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-title">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">BEFORE SETUP</p>
        <h2 id="lifecycle-title">What becoming a Reviewer means</h2>
        <p>
          You publish your own Review Policy, receive public Review Requests,
          decide when to review, and record outcomes that can make your GitHub
          Stars explainable.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}how-it-works/`}>
          Understand the Review and Re-review lifecycle
        </a>
      </div>
      <ol class="lifecycle-steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Own your Policy</strong>
          <span>Define your standard in README.md.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Receive Review Requests</strong>
          <span>Repository owners ask for evaluation, not for a Star.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Choose how to review</strong>
          <span>Review manually, start gh shoal locally, or explicitly opt in to scheduled Hosted Review.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Back PASS with evidence</strong>
          <span>A valid PASS may turn your real Star into a public endorsement.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <Join serviceUrl={joinServiceUrl} client:load />

    <section class="join-reference" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
      <h2 id="trust-title">How Policy, trust, and Automated Review work</h2>
      <div>
        <section>
          <h3>Your Review Policy</h3>
          <p>You define your own standard in <code>README.md</code>. Setup leaves Policy authorship to you. Manual Review is valid when formal Review / Re-review results follow the recognized Protocol format.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Shoal-managed station surfaces</h3>
          <p><code>.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/review-request.yml</code> and <code>.github/workflows/reviewer-summary.yml</code> are Shoal-managed. Even whitespace or comments change the workflow’s exact digest; a Summary outside the allowed canonical digest set is rejected. Run <code>gh shoal init</code> to repair managed-file drift. In local setup, a fresh fork’s Actions confirmation remains yours to complete. Quick Web Join can enable the required Actions state after your explicit authorization.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Choose your review execution</h3>
          <p>Run <code>gh shoal</code> with an explicitly selected local agent: <code>claude</code>, <code>codex</code>, <code>gemini</code>, <code>opencode</code>, <code>cursor</code>, <code>grok</code>, <code>qwen</code>, or <code>kimi</code>. Local / CLI execution uses your own credentials and remains independent. You can also explicitly enable Hosted Copilot Review in the settings above with a separate recurring authorization. Both paths use the shared Review runtime and Protocol. Operational failures leave work pending; they do not create FAIL judgments.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
